.angular
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees
.playwright-mcp

# Vendored agent skills. `npx skills add` writes the trees under `.agents/skills/` and links
# them into each configured tool's directory; `skills-lock.json` records the source and the
# digest, and `npx skills experimental_install` restores them from it. The LOCKFILE is
# tracked and the
# payload is not — the same split as `package-lock.json` and `node_modules`, for the same
# reason (decision 0040): a copy of somebody else's documentation ages from the moment it
# lands, and no tool configured here reads `.agents/` at all. `.claude/skills/` is ignored
# whole, because `.claude/settings.json` already says where that tool takes its workspace
# skills from; under `.opencode/skills/` the vendored names are listed one by one, because
# the skills of THIS repository live there and are tracked.
/.agents/
/.claude/skills/
/.opencode/skills/angular-developer
/.opencode/skills/angular-new-app

# The language gate's word lists, restored out of `tools/dictionaries.lock.json` by
# `tools/restore-dictionaries.mjs` and verified against its hashes on every run. The
# LOCKFILE is tracked and the 62 MB of somebody else's word lists are not — the same
# split as above, for the same reason (decision 0040).
/tools/.dictionaries/

vite.config.*.timestamp*
vitest.config.*.timestamp*

.nx/polygraph
.nx/self-healing
.nx/migrate-runs

# Playwright's run ledger (`.last-run.json`), written to the invoking directory even for a
# run whose config lives elsewhere. Nothing reads it back here.
/test-results/

# Visual test baselines (apps/sandbox-e2e/src/__screenshots__) ARE in the repository
# and have to stay: without them Playwright records a baseline on the first run and
# stores it as correct, so the gate can never fire. Only the output of a failed
# comparison is ignored (the actual image and the diff), which is written to the
# run's output directory.
*-actual.png
*-diff.png

# Notes that must not reach the public repository. `docs/` is a public surface from the
# first push on, so commercial reasoning sits next to it rather than inside it — decisions
# 0015 and 0016 carry only what may be read from outside. The directory is UNTRACKED:
# git neither copies it nor restores it after `clean -xdf`.
/docs/private/
